    "narrative": "With the season nearing its conclusion, our lineup for September 24th is anchored by two high-efficiency leadoff hitters, **Drake Baldwin** (68.70) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67). Both benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.50\u2014Singer and Dobnak, respectively\u2014making them our most reliable sources for runs today. While the mid-order stalwarts like **Kyle Tucker** (53.77) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.51) face tougher tests against Glasnow and Pivetta, their elite profiles remain start-worthy despite the stiff competition. **Heliot Ramos** (46.65) is a specific tactical play here; while his raw score is moderate, his matchup against the left-handed Seymour provides a rare speed-related edge, as the opposing hurler's slow delivery should theoretically grant **Heliot Ramos** a higher probability of success on the basepaths\u2014a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler**, whose 39.36 score narrowly missed the 40-point efficiency floor. While **Wade Meckler** benefits from a strong batting order placement, the combination of a less-than-ideal park and a formidable matchup against Woo relegated him to the bench in favor of preserving game caps. Elsewhere, we continue to manage the absences of core contributors **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson**, both of whom are sidelined today, while **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Liam Hicks** (42.88) and **Brayan Rocchio** (43.50); both are trending toward the lower end of our starting threshold. **Brayan Rocchio** specifically faces a wind-in scenario that dampens his power potential, and we will monitor weather updates closely, as any shift in wind velocity could further depress his efficiency against Suarez.",
